WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.194 --> 00:00:02.702
- For a long time,
people were talking about

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:06.138
bullying and that was a big hot topic

00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:07.735
and I think sometimes you can forget

00:00:07.735 --> 00:00:09.808
that you could be your
own bully in some ways.

00:00:09.808 --> 00:00:11.896
You don't have to be
born into a situation,

00:00:11.896 --> 00:00:13.254
you don't have to come from something,

00:00:13.254 --> 00:00:15.659
or possess something, or look flawless,

00:00:15.659 --> 00:00:17.508
even though I like looking
like this sometimes.

00:00:17.508 --> 00:00:19.897
If you can believe in something great,

00:00:19.897 --> 00:00:22.223
I feel like you can
achieve something great.

00:00:22.223 --> 00:00:24.664
- She's an American singer and songwriter.

00:00:24.664 --> 00:00:27.072
She's one of the best
selling musicians of all time

00:00:27.072 --> 00:00:30.297
having sold over 100
million albums worldwide.

00:00:30.297 --> 00:00:33.779
Her estimated net worth is $125 million.

00:00:33.779 --> 00:00:35.444
She's Katy Perry and here's my take

00:00:35.444 --> 00:00:37.316
on her top ten rules of success.

00:00:37.316 --> 00:00:38.900
Rule number five is my personal favorite

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:39.980
and make sure to stick around all the way

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:41.733
to the end for a special bonus clip.

00:00:41.733 --> 00:00:42.924
Also, as Katy is talking,

00:00:42.924 --> 00:00:45.137
if she says something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:45.137 --> 00:00:46.583
please leave it in the comments below

00:00:46.583 --> 00:00:47.546
and put quotes around it,

00:00:47.546 --> 00:00:49.937
so other people can be inspired as well.

00:00:49.937 --> 00:00:50.836
Enjoy.

00:00:50.836 --> 00:00:51.892
(blasting off)

00:00:51.892 --> 00:00:53.657
(exploding)

00:00:53.657 --> 00:00:56.324
(uptempo music)

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:06.138
- For a long time,
people were talking about

00:01:06.138 --> 00:01:09.652
bullying and that was a big hot topic

00:01:09.652 --> 00:01:11.266
and I think sometimes you can forget

00:01:11.266 --> 00:01:13.355
that you could be your
own bully in some ways.

00:01:13.355 --> 00:01:15.349
Like you are the person that is standing

00:01:15.349 --> 00:01:16.911
in the way of your success,

00:01:16.911 --> 00:01:19.376
whether it's professionally or personally,

00:01:19.376 --> 00:01:22.605
and, honestly, that was the case for me.

00:01:22.605 --> 00:01:24.922
I was having a great professional streak,

00:01:24.922 --> 00:01:27.102
but personally I was really immature,

00:01:27.102 --> 00:01:29.191
and so I had to balance them out.

00:01:29.191 --> 00:01:31.044
Finally, I had enough and I said,

00:01:31.044 --> 00:01:33.275
"Hey, you need to speak up for yourself.

00:01:33.275 --> 00:01:34.573
"If you're not happy with something,

00:01:34.573 --> 00:01:35.406
"you change it."

00:01:35.406 --> 00:01:37.741
"Change it, make yourself
better every single day,

00:01:37.741 --> 00:01:41.199
"so I went to a lot of therapy (laughs)

00:01:41.199 --> 00:01:44.691
"and I guess I put it in the way of like

00:01:44.691 --> 00:01:46.382
"'you're going to hear me wear,' finally,

00:01:46.382 --> 00:01:48.724
"I'm going to be able
to speak up for myself."

00:01:48.724 --> 00:01:52.891
This next record that I'll
start in a couple of months,

00:01:54.323 --> 00:01:55.846
I think it'll be, actually, more honest

00:01:55.846 --> 00:01:57.211
because I think when you get older,

00:01:57.211 --> 00:02:00.311
you care less what people think about you

00:02:00.311 --> 00:02:03.969
and I have had to really work on that.

00:02:03.969 --> 00:02:05.329
I think that's one of the biggest things

00:02:05.329 --> 00:02:07.588
you have to work on when you
are put into the spotlight

00:02:07.588 --> 00:02:10.072
is not caring about what
people say about you

00:02:10.072 --> 00:02:13.739
because you just become this open forum

00:02:13.739 --> 00:02:16.156
to anybody, anything, anyone,

00:02:17.195 --> 00:02:20.042
and if you start reading your own press,

00:02:20.042 --> 00:02:21.407
it will ruin you.

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:23.073
I feel like I've got the opportunity

00:02:23.073 --> 00:02:24.337
to make more of a career rather than

00:02:24.337 --> 00:02:27.532
just like a flash in the pan,

00:02:27.532 --> 00:02:29.579
she's hot, she's not type of thing,

00:02:29.579 --> 00:02:31.510
but that's only because
I have worked so hard

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:34.165
and focused and everything I do,

00:02:34.165 --> 00:02:36.240
I know it's for the fans

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.331
and they're the reason why I exist.

00:02:38.331 --> 00:02:41.550
- Tell me about why you
decided to do this documentary.

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:42.387
- Oh, my goodness.

00:02:42.387 --> 00:02:43.739
Well, I always liked to be honest

00:02:43.739 --> 00:02:46.320
with everything I do, especially my songs.

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:48.557
I like to plant those
seeds of honesty and truth

00:02:48.557 --> 00:02:49.470
because we live in a world

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:51.804
that doesn't have much of that left.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:56.152
And with this documentary,
I wanted to show people

00:02:56.152 --> 00:02:58.150
what was underneath the hood

00:02:58.150 --> 00:02:59.403
and you can attest to that.

00:02:59.403 --> 00:03:00.822
I've been under the hood many times.

00:03:00.822 --> 00:03:03.137
(audience laughing)

00:03:03.137 --> 00:03:04.504
I really wanted to show people

00:03:04.504 --> 00:03:07.061
how much hard work it takes,

00:03:07.061 --> 00:03:09.447
the ins and outs, and how, really,

00:03:09.447 --> 00:03:11.529
you don't have to be
born into a situation,

00:03:11.529 --> 00:03:12.871
you don't have to come from something,

00:03:12.871 --> 00:03:15.265
or possess something, or look flawless,

00:03:15.265 --> 00:03:17.817
even though I like looking
like this sometimes.

00:03:17.817 --> 00:03:20.701
You can just be you and have a dream

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:22.780
and plant the seed and water the root.

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:26.341
I found a lot of self-love this year

00:03:26.341 --> 00:03:28.591
and I rebuilt my confidence

00:03:29.432 --> 00:03:32.788
that had had a little
bit of a shatter to it.

00:03:32.788 --> 00:03:36.453
And I went inwards rather
than pointing the finger

00:03:36.453 --> 00:03:38.685
on everyone else and blaming everyone

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:42.506
for my problems or the issues that I had.

00:03:42.506 --> 00:03:46.764
I went inwards and tried
to do some patchwork.

00:03:46.764 --> 00:03:49.135
To heal up little spots
that I needed to heal up

00:03:49.135 --> 00:03:53.252
or say to myself, "What
can I do to make myself

00:03:53.252 --> 00:03:54.488
"a better human representation--"

00:03:54.488 --> 00:03:55.324
- What did you do?

00:03:55.324 --> 00:03:57.100
- I did a lot of different things.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:00.154
I did a cleanse for three months

00:04:00.154 --> 00:04:02.662
that I didn't have any alcohol

00:04:02.662 --> 00:04:05.329
and I did a whole vitamin regime

00:04:06.275 --> 00:04:10.181
and I wen to therapy,
I did more mediation.

00:04:10.181 --> 00:04:11.926
I've been meditating
for a couple years now,

00:04:11.926 --> 00:04:13.843
but I upped it.

00:04:13.843 --> 00:04:16.115
And I just went the positive route

00:04:16.115 --> 00:04:17.972
rather than going to the club

00:04:17.972 --> 00:04:19.881
and getting drunk every night (laughs).

00:04:19.881 --> 00:04:22.265
I mean I've probably done
that a couple of times,

00:04:22.265 --> 00:04:25.573
but I really serve myself well

00:04:25.573 --> 00:04:27.795
and it influenced all of my songwriting

00:04:27.795 --> 00:04:29.754
and I wrote most of the
songs during this time.

00:04:29.754 --> 00:04:33.342
From the very beginning of
me getting into the industry,

00:04:33.342 --> 00:04:37.259
I would be out and about
and I would hear girls

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:42.445
or actresses, or musicians, or whatever.

00:04:43.321 --> 00:04:44.565
They would say, "Oh, no, I don't want

00:04:44.565 --> 00:04:45.488
"to be in a relationship

00:04:45.488 --> 00:04:46.861
"because I don't want to have to choose

00:04:46.861 --> 00:04:48.971
"between being in a relationship

00:04:48.971 --> 00:04:50.448
"and having a career,"

00:04:50.448 --> 00:04:55.281
and I thought to myself (blows),

00:04:55.281 --> 00:04:57.811
"When I find that person

00:04:57.811 --> 00:05:00.561
"that's going to be my life partner,

00:05:01.417 --> 00:05:02.959
"I won't ever have to choose

00:05:02.959 --> 00:05:05.476
"because they'll be accepting of me

00:05:05.476 --> 00:05:07.244
"completely for who I am."

00:05:07.244 --> 00:05:11.397
Not me being able to
just do whatever I want,

00:05:11.397 --> 00:05:14.682
necessarily, but they wont' be threatened

00:05:14.682 --> 00:05:17.515
or have weird motives or whatever.

00:05:18.972 --> 00:05:21.114
They will be accepting of me,

00:05:21.114 --> 00:05:23.640
the things I love, the ambition,

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:27.225
what I aspire to be,
what I want to create.

00:05:27.225 --> 00:05:29.186
They'll be accepting and supportive.

00:05:29.186 --> 00:05:30.265
And then I started to realize,

00:05:30.265 --> 00:05:31.265
"Oh, my God.

00:05:33.157 --> 00:05:34.515
"That's not true.

00:05:34.515 --> 00:05:38.682
"That fairytale that I had is
not true for me right now."

00:05:40.918 --> 00:05:41.751
Yeah.

00:05:42.825 --> 00:05:43.658
I don't want--

00:05:43.658 --> 00:05:45.908
(exhaling)

00:05:52.768 --> 00:05:54.244
- [Announcer] Okay, again, everyone.

00:05:54.244 --> 00:05:56.411
(mumbles)

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:02.270
- I'll tell ya' the truth is that

00:06:04.159 --> 00:06:05.796
I'm a romantic

00:06:05.796 --> 00:06:08.379
and I believe in this fairytale

00:06:11.715 --> 00:06:12.579
and in some ways I think

00:06:12.579 --> 00:06:14.957
that's always been to my advantage

00:06:14.957 --> 00:06:18.122
because if you can believe
in something great,

00:06:18.122 --> 00:06:21.788
I feel like you can
achieve something great.

00:06:21.788 --> 00:06:25.821
I have that same belief
system with everything

00:06:25.821 --> 00:06:27.738
from career to my life,

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:32.436
my personal life, everything,

00:06:32.436 --> 00:06:34.721
and I will do everything it takes

00:06:34.721 --> 00:06:38.443
to not fail and I did everything it took,

00:06:38.443 --> 00:06:40.110
but it still failed.

00:06:42.152 --> 00:06:44.085
The bad that comes along with the good

00:06:44.085 --> 00:06:47.954
is a journey and I learned
so much from that journey.

00:06:47.954 --> 00:06:49.553
- Why did you decide to
come out with "Roar"?

00:06:49.553 --> 00:06:52.264
There was that big countdown
and then "Roar" came out

00:06:52.264 --> 00:06:53.474
and it was huge for you.

00:06:53.474 --> 00:06:55.155
You broke your own records there.

00:06:55.155 --> 00:06:57.462
Why was it "Roar" the first single?

00:06:57.462 --> 00:07:00.526
- It was up for debate,
a couple of singles.

00:07:00.526 --> 00:07:03.609
It was going to be "Roar" or another one

00:07:04.559 --> 00:07:06.786
and we decided to go with "Roar"

00:07:06.786 --> 00:07:09.827
because of the reaction I
was getting from my friends.

00:07:09.827 --> 00:07:11.410
I use my friends as

00:07:13.072 --> 00:07:13.905
guinea pigs.

00:07:13.905 --> 00:07:15.222
As test guinea pigs

00:07:15.222 --> 00:07:19.389
and I have a very eclectic
group of friends ranging from

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:24.644
DJs to artists to just moms (laughs)

00:07:24.644 --> 00:07:28.148
and they all really agreed that "Roar"

00:07:28.148 --> 00:07:32.545
was the best one and it
has that bouncy feel.

00:07:32.545 --> 00:07:35.409
That 8th note feel, but
it also has this message

00:07:35.409 --> 00:07:37.672
of finding your inner strength again

00:07:37.672 --> 00:07:40.045
and letting that come out as a roar

00:07:40.045 --> 00:07:41.712
and people related to it.

00:07:41.712 --> 00:07:42.607
- Yeah, well, they really did--

00:07:42.607 --> 00:07:43.495
- And there's something.

00:07:43.495 --> 00:07:45.887
There's an intuitive thing that happens

00:07:45.887 --> 00:07:48.622
inside of me and I've
always trust my intuition

00:07:48.622 --> 00:07:50.824
when it comes to writing songs

00:07:50.824 --> 00:07:53.689
and picking which songs
should come out as singles.

00:07:53.689 --> 00:07:55.247
I've been on tour for a year

00:07:55.247 --> 00:07:58.460
and before that, I did promo for my record

00:07:58.460 --> 00:08:01.653
and my record almost
came out two years ago,

00:08:01.653 --> 00:08:03.440
so I've been doing a lot of work for that

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:05.270
for the past couple years and I think

00:08:05.270 --> 00:08:07.071
what would be most important for me

00:08:07.071 --> 00:08:10.937
is to, at this moment, gather my thoughts

00:08:10.937 --> 00:08:14.187
and live a little bit of life on my own

00:08:15.161 --> 00:08:17.659
and not around a traveling circus

00:08:17.659 --> 00:08:20.616
of a hundred people and have quiet moments

00:08:20.616 --> 00:08:22.283
and ride my bike and

00:08:24.909 --> 00:08:25.876
find my roots again.

00:08:25.876 --> 00:08:28.950
That's what I always do in between records

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:32.623
is I go to a quiet place
and restore my soul.

00:08:32.623 --> 00:08:35.290
(uptempo music)

00:08:41.136 --> 00:08:43.863
I usually go back to my
hometown of Santa Barbara

00:08:43.863 --> 00:08:47.666
and figure out what all of this means

00:08:47.666 --> 00:08:49.147
and get away from the distraction

00:08:49.147 --> 00:08:52.147
and feed my spirituality and feed my

00:08:54.488 --> 00:08:55.321
music.

00:08:55.321 --> 00:08:58.321
Listening to a lot of music and just

00:08:59.766 --> 00:09:02.293
getting my feet planted
back on the ground again.

00:09:02.293 --> 00:09:04.960
(uptempo music)

00:09:08.746 --> 00:09:11.297
It's really important for me to live life,

00:09:11.297 --> 00:09:14.684
absorb life, and have my own experiences,

00:09:14.684 --> 00:09:16.997
so that I can go back to the drawing board

00:09:16.997 --> 00:09:19.708
and have something authentic to say.

00:09:19.708 --> 00:09:22.847
- Question to Katy Perry
via YouTube moderator.

00:09:22.847 --> 00:09:25.374
How was life before
you became a celebrity?

00:09:25.374 --> 00:09:27.045
Before your big break?

00:09:27.045 --> 00:09:28.793
- He's got the creepy voice a little bit.

00:09:28.793 --> 00:09:29.974
- That's okay.

00:09:29.974 --> 00:09:31.196
We don't judge.

00:09:31.196 --> 00:09:32.442
I could be creepy too.

00:09:32.442 --> 00:09:34.096
I mean if you saw me in a purple wig

00:09:34.096 --> 00:09:37.997
walking down the street
you'd be like, "Freak!"

00:09:37.997 --> 00:09:41.123
Well, it was all about
the hustle and the bustle

00:09:41.123 --> 00:09:44.850
and sometimes it was me tryin' to keep up

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:47.267
with the Jones', as they say.

00:09:48.593 --> 00:09:50.997
I wanted to be seen like I was worth it

00:09:50.997 --> 00:09:53.664
and so I was trying to always be

00:09:55.611 --> 00:09:59.111
ready for a opportunity to present itself.

00:10:00.613 --> 00:10:01.753
It was exciting.

00:10:01.753 --> 00:10:05.951
It was a little bit not as
fast paced as it is now.

00:10:05.951 --> 00:10:09.181
Things are just so fast
paced like lightning speed

00:10:09.181 --> 00:10:11.127
and I know what I'm doing today

00:10:11.127 --> 00:10:13.951
and I know what I'm doing, probably,

00:10:13.951 --> 00:10:16.433
in six months to the date,

00:10:16.433 --> 00:10:18.730
so it wasn't as scheduled,

00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:20.962
but I think I had a little bit

00:10:20.962 --> 00:10:22.035
more time on my hands,

00:10:22.035 --> 00:10:23.905
but I think that maybe I might've gotten

00:10:23.905 --> 00:10:25.863
into a little bit more trouble back then

00:10:25.863 --> 00:10:27.530
because, what is it?

00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:31.388
Idle hands are the devil's workshop

00:10:31.388 --> 00:10:33.156
is what my parents said,

00:10:33.156 --> 00:10:36.959
so now I really have
a lot to take care of,

00:10:36.959 --> 00:10:40.658
but it was just about working on my craft

00:10:40.658 --> 00:10:43.158
and making sure that it was perfect,

00:10:43.158 --> 00:10:47.217
so that when finally I
would get that opportunity,

00:10:47.217 --> 00:10:48.227
I'd be ready for it.

00:10:48.227 --> 00:10:51.527
♫ This is the part of me

00:10:51.527 --> 00:10:53.004
- [Interviewer] Do you
steal believe in love?

00:10:53.004 --> 00:10:54.004
- Of course!

00:10:55.712 --> 00:10:59.448
I'm going to let love
lead the way, always,

00:10:59.448 --> 00:11:02.371
and I was born with this blind ambition

00:11:02.371 --> 00:11:04.524
and it's gotten me here to this point

00:11:04.524 --> 00:11:07.160
and I think that I'll stick to it.

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:08.266
So, yes.

00:11:08.266 --> 00:11:09.099
Oh, mom!

00:11:10.892 --> 00:11:11.877
- [Mom] Huh?

00:11:11.877 --> 00:11:13.408
- You're on speakerphone

00:11:13.408 --> 00:11:15.448
and I'm on the stage right now.

00:11:15.448 --> 00:11:18.448
(audience cheering)

00:11:20.986 --> 00:11:25.514
And we all just want to wish
you a happy Mother's Day!

00:11:25.514 --> 00:11:28.900
(audience cheering)

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:30.068
- [Mom] You're my little feather.

00:11:30.068 --> 00:11:31.067
- Okay.

00:11:31.067 --> 00:11:31.900
(audience laughing)

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:32.733
- [Audience Member] What
did she say (laughs)?

00:11:32.733 --> 00:11:33.566
- [Katy] I'm your little feather.

00:11:33.566 --> 00:11:34.399
I love you, mom.

00:11:34.399 --> 00:11:35.383
I have to continue with the show,

00:11:35.383 --> 00:11:38.403
but I just wanted to wish
you happy Mother's Day.

00:11:38.403 --> 00:11:39.616
- [Mom] Alright, I love you too.

00:11:39.616 --> 00:11:40.449
See you soon.

00:11:40.449 --> 00:11:41.837
Bye bye, everybody.

00:11:41.837 --> 00:11:43.561
- [Katy] What?

00:11:43.561 --> 00:11:44.815
- Bye bye, everyone.

00:11:44.815 --> 00:11:46.232
- [Audience] Bye!

00:11:47.332 --> 00:11:49.055
- Bye, mom.

00:11:49.055 --> 00:11:52.055
(audience cheering)

00:11:56.410 --> 00:11:57.758
- Thank you guys so much for watching!

00:11:57.758 --> 00:12:01.271
I made this video because
unlimited traffic asked me to,

00:12:01.271 --> 00:12:02.458
so if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:12:02.458 --> 00:12:04.085
that you want me to profile next,

00:12:04.085 --> 00:12:05.558
please leave it down in the comments below

00:12:05.558 --> 00:12:06.683
and I'll see what I can do.

00:12:06.683 --> 00:12:07.841
I also love to know what did you take

00:12:07.841 --> 00:12:10.340
from Katy that had the
biggest impact on you.

00:12:10.340 --> 00:12:11.286
What lesson are you going to apply

00:12:11.286 --> 00:12:12.681
to your business or your life?

00:12:12.681 --> 00:12:13.754
Please leave it in the comments

00:12:13.754 --> 00:12:15.262
(mumbles) join in the discussion.

00:12:15.262 --> 00:12:16.376
Also, want to give a quick shoutout

00:12:16.376 --> 00:12:18.767
to my sister, Stefanie Carmichael.

00:12:18.767 --> 00:12:20.173
Thank you so much for picking up a copy

00:12:20.173 --> 00:12:23.067
of my book and also going to the bookstore

00:12:23.067 --> 00:12:25.659
and rearranging it, so that
my book comes up first.

00:12:25.659 --> 00:12:26.642
I really appreciate that.

00:12:26.642 --> 00:12:27.475
Thanks for the love.

00:12:27.475 --> 00:12:29.225
So, thank you guys again for watching.

00:12:29.225 --> 00:12:30.568
I believe in you.

00:12:30.568 --> 00:12:32.820
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:12:32.820 --> 00:12:35.448
and whatever your one word is.

00:12:35.448 --> 00:12:36.603
Much love.

00:12:36.603 --> 00:12:37.711
I'll see ya' soon.

00:12:37.711 --> 00:12:39.036
(blasting off)

00:12:39.036 --> 00:12:40.161
(exploding)

00:12:40.161 --> 00:12:42.244
(flying)

00:12:43.676 --> 00:12:46.509
- Transcendental mediation, to me,

00:12:48.917 --> 00:12:50.989
it's like a great workout

00:12:50.989 --> 00:12:53.075
for your mind without working out,

00:12:53.075 --> 00:12:56.658
but you get all the
effects of working out.

00:12:57.656 --> 00:12:59.979
I come from a very spiritual world,

00:12:59.979 --> 00:13:02.194
from a very religious upbringing,

00:13:02.194 --> 00:13:06.181
and it's not religious,
it's not spiritual,

00:13:06.181 --> 00:13:07.513
although I think if you're taking care

00:13:07.513 --> 00:13:11.462
of you body, your mind,
that is a spiritual thing,

00:13:11.462 --> 00:13:15.051
but it doesn't have that
religious background.

00:13:15.051 --> 00:13:17.468
To me it's mostly medical and

00:13:18.874 --> 00:13:22.207
it's like a little pill, but not a pill.

00:13:23.621 --> 00:13:25.129
It's a practice, so it's a little

00:13:25.129 --> 00:13:27.212
practice that you do and,

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:31.627
to me, it's the most rest.

00:13:32.494 --> 00:13:35.969
It's the most power
nap you could ever get.

00:13:35.969 --> 00:13:38.188
- And that experience of that quiet.

00:13:38.188 --> 00:13:40.202
That is, they call it,

00:13:40.202 --> 00:13:42.832
state of restful alertness,
according to science.

00:13:42.832 --> 00:13:44.823
Where your mind is completely settled,

00:13:44.823 --> 00:13:48.342
but you're wide awake
and it's before thoughts.

00:13:48.342 --> 00:13:50.295
Someone said to me, "Well, how do you know

00:13:50.295 --> 00:13:51.155
"when your 20 minutes are up?"

00:13:51.155 --> 00:13:53.237
I said, "Well, you can
look at your watch."

00:13:53.237 --> 00:13:54.686
It's not like you're going someplace,

00:13:54.686 --> 00:13:57.454
but that peaceful state that you access

00:13:57.454 --> 00:13:59.415
just happened quite effortlessly

00:13:59.415 --> 00:14:02.332
and that's a wonderful description.

00:14:04.156 --> 00:14:05.298
Oh, one more question.

00:14:05.298 --> 00:14:09.405
How do you think it's impacted
your remarkable career?

00:14:09.405 --> 00:14:11.730
- My life is so crazy.

00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:12.828
It really is.

00:14:12.828 --> 00:14:14.160
It's extreme.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:17.327
I live in this one percentile extreme.

00:14:18.738 --> 00:14:20.077
I'm zigzagging all over the world.

00:14:20.077 --> 00:14:22.578
I'm on a plane more than I am on ground

00:14:22.578 --> 00:14:26.683
and this tool helps me
find moments of peace

00:14:26.683 --> 00:14:28.857
because I don't have a whole lot of time

00:14:28.857 --> 00:14:33.024
that extend my day, so I can
live my fullest capacity.

00:14:34.133 --> 00:14:36.693
It gives me two days in one day.

00:14:36.693 --> 00:14:38.695
It just gives me this power.

00:14:38.695 --> 00:14:42.362
And I do it before I
write a song sometimes,

00:14:43.603 --> 00:14:45.618
definitely before I get on stage,

00:14:45.618 --> 00:14:49.067
and it's just such an incredible, useful,

00:14:49.067 --> 00:14:51.150
simple tool that has made

00:14:52.068 --> 00:14:53.848
such an impact on me and that's why

00:14:53.848 --> 00:14:55.964
I'm sitting here with you today.

00:14:55.964 --> 00:14:58.484
- You're very calm on tour.

00:14:58.484 --> 00:15:00.598
At least with me 'cause you invited

00:15:00.598 --> 00:15:05.226
our whole team to come and
teach your team to meditate

00:15:05.226 --> 00:15:09.053
and I ran into you, you're
coming out of a room

00:15:09.053 --> 00:15:10.797
and we're just chatting and you looked

00:15:10.797 --> 00:15:14.977
and you said, "Bob, there's
16,000 people waiting for me.

00:15:14.977 --> 00:15:16.039
"Right around the corner."

00:15:16.039 --> 00:15:18.147
And you just did that,
you were polite with me,

00:15:18.147 --> 00:15:19.524
and you just waked out on the stage,

00:15:19.524 --> 00:15:21.538
but there was such an evenness.

00:15:21.538 --> 00:15:23.943
- I'm a multitasker (laughs).

00:15:23.943 --> 00:15:26.093
- [Man] You have a great deal
of kindness inside of you.

00:15:26.093 --> 00:15:28.646
- Thank you.
- You're a very kind person.

00:15:28.646 --> 00:15:29.512
- Thank you.

00:15:29.512 --> 00:15:32.317
I think that it would be a shame

00:15:32.317 --> 00:15:35.734
to have such a great cure all to yourself

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:39.668
like the cure for the common cold

00:15:39.668 --> 00:15:41.005
and not to share it with people

00:15:41.005 --> 00:15:42.583
that are suffering.

00:15:42.583 --> 00:15:45.056
So, it's the cure for the common stress,

00:15:45.056 --> 00:15:48.504
which stress is a killer these days

00:15:48.504 --> 00:15:50.482
and I have a lot of it in my life

00:15:50.482 --> 00:15:54.232
and I have a great tool
that helps subside it

00:15:55.467 --> 00:15:56.665
and I want to share that

00:15:56.665 --> 00:15:58.091
'cause I don't want people to suffer.

00:15:58.091 --> 00:15:59.328
I like to lift people up.

